      "explanation": "Exception RD 18 sets site-specific rules for detached houses: a maximum height of 8.5 m with a peak roof or 6.0 m with a flat roof; a 6.0 m main wall height limit on either the front and rear walls or the side walls; a gross floor area cap of the greater of 185 m2 or 0.45 times the lot area (counting garages and double-counted void areas, with up to 4% of void area excluded); side yard setbacks for houses of 2 or more storeys that grow with lot frontage; a garage for 3 or more cars only on lots wider than 27.0 m; and, on lots narrower than 12.0 m, at most 3.0 m of combined vehicle entrance width in the front wall. The building-depth measurement includes the one-storey extension. No prevailing by-laws apply.",
      "code_refs": "none"
    },
    "900.3.10(254)": {
      "explanation": "Exception RD 254 sets a minimum side yard setback of 0.9 m and a minimum setback of 3.6 m from a side lot line that abuts a street, and requires the lands to also comply with exception RD 1462. No prevailing by-laws apply.",
      "code_refs": "none"
    }
  }
}
